sfire iron man uses sonic weapons to  knock out the agents  and then captures the final mandroid  after the pilot eject some fleece  when fury later accuses stark of  betraying him tony produces a bug that  iron man had supposedly planted on him  thereby sidestepping any guilt for his  role in shield's defeat  at this point in time steve rogers has  been forced to give up his captain  america identity by the government  in response he simply starts calling  himself the captain  and turns to tony stark for a new shield  stark is more than happy to help of  course  hoping that if steve owes him a favor he  might just stay out of his way in return  sadly that plan doesn't quite work out  and the captain quickly gets his stark's  next target  the guardsmen an elite squad who guards  a supervillain prison known as  the vault the captain catches stark  before he can bluff his way in however  so stark beats the hasty retreat luckily  stark has a new plan  he has jim rhodes pretend to be electro  in order to get sent to the vault  once inside rhodes shuts down the  defenses and floods the place with  knockout gas  brodie and iron man then disable 40  suits of guardsman armor  luckily most of them were off-duty  leaving just half a dozen still able to  put up a fight  iron man is about to deal with the last  one before the captain who has  anticipated iron man's break-in  finally steps in while the captain helps  to down guardsmen  iron man takes the opportunity to  immobilize him with electricity  while iron man succeeds in his mission  this confrontation with rogers marks the  beginning of a rift  that would only widen over the coming  years finally culminating in the  devastating civil war storyline  almost 20 years later unfortunately iron  man's actions at the vault  inadvertently lead to the breakout of  several high-profile prisoners  subsequently hawkeye tells iron man that  his vendetta must come to an end  but stark well pretty much just ignores  him by this point 